I only have a few items to take to task.<P>Spell interruption - <BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif">quote:</font><HR>Make sure you are at a dead stop before you start.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Best way to do this is when you stop running, "TAP" one of your turn keys, be it the left or right arrow, or what ever you have it mapped to. Just a tap, this sends a signal to the EQ servers that you have change directions, oh and hey look you stopped to.<P>Specialization - <BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif">quote:</font><HR>If you are going to quad kite, you must specialize in Evocation.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Ok this one just plain upsets me. No you don't need to. I went with Alteration, I wanted to be a grouping druid. Alteration helps me get those extra heals off when they are most needed. Or now, since those heals took less mana I now still have enough to pull an evac off. <P>I think thats all that I see, I'll reread it again, so I might find more.   <IMG SRC="wink.gif" border="0"><P>--------------------<P><B>Nefarius Draconocissor</B> - 54 Wanderer/Freelance Gynocologist <BR><B>Meretrixx</B> - 48 Warrior<BR>Division 13<BR>Bertoxxolus<P> <img src="http://www.users.qwest.net/~portermichael/eq/sig.jpg"> 
